{"primary_source_ids":["G00013"],"context_source_ids":[],"context_limitations":["G00012: adjacent context exceeds budget; boundary review required","G00014: adjacent context exceeds budget; boundary review required","G00013: ASR speech evidence; exact code/formula unavailable unless separately verified."],"excerpts":[{"ref":"Q0000","source_id":"G00013","quote":"for domestic goods and the domestic demand for goods, OK?","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0001","source_id":"G00013","quote":"I know it's going to be tricky.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0002","source_id":"G00013","quote":"But there's an difference between demand
 for domestic goods versus the domestic demand for goods.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0003","source_id":"G00013","quote":"This is what residents, say US residents,
 household, firms, government, demand in terms of goods.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0004","source_id":"G00013","quote":"This is how those same agents plus the rest of the world
 demand of domestically produced goods.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0005","source_id":"G00013","quote":"That's the distinction.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0006","source_id":"G00013","quote":"When the economy was closed, they were the same.","role":"primary"}],"ingestion_binding":"e39ce56bd8515adc4ada76fb824776b312b834efde9dd2d209dc544422bdc714"}

{"primary_source_ids":["G00015"],"context_source_ids":[],"context_limitations":["G00014: adjacent context exceeds budget; boundary review required","G00016: adjacent context exceeds budget; boundary review required","G00015: ASR speech evidence; exact code/formula unavailable unless separately verified."],"excerpts":[{"ref":"Q0000","source_id":"G00015","quote":"That's not the demand for domestic production
 and therefore will not be determined at equilibrium output domestically.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0001","source_id":"G00015","quote":"So this is going to be a new concept, which is demand for domestic goods.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0002","source_id":"G00015","quote":"And for domestic goods, it's the same as domestic demand
 for goods, that, the thing we had in closed economy,
 minus that part of demand that is satisfied by input.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0003","source_id":"G00015","quote":"So minus input, and divided by the exchanger,
 because inputs may be priced in euros,
 say, and I had to convert them into dollars.","role":"primary"},{"ref":"Q0004","source_id":"G00015","quote":"That's the reason it's divided","role":"primary"}],"ingestion_binding":"e39ce56bd8515adc4ada76fb824776b312b834efde9dd2d209dc544422bdc714"}
